# estige exit node — Termux package env file.
#
# Sourced by $PREFIX/var/service/estige/run before it execs the binary. The
# file is the env chain for a packaged service: the binary reads no file.
# Keep it mode 0600.
#
# NOTHING SECRET LIVES HERE (d236). The host identity, the admitted relays and
# the egress policy are the store under $XDG_DATA_HOME/estige (default
# ~/.local/share/estige):
#
#   estige keygen -principal <name>          # mint this host's key + certificate
#   cat ~/.local/share/estige/relay.json     # paste the {name, public} row
#   estige key check                         # load both role files like boot does
#
# Without a store the exit node refuses to start — that is the kill switch
# (docs/d084/d236): there is no env fallback and older env spellings fail
# closed.
#
# Bind (docs/d110): a bare port number, unset = 8080 on all interfaces.
# PORT=8080
#
# A second, capped-edge listener (docs/d222): the port a Cloudflare (or other
# body-capping edge) connector points at, where h2-post-unbounded is refused at
# request initiation and only h2-post-windowed serves.
# PORT_CLOUDFLARE=8081
#
# The store root, when it is not the XDG default.
# XDG_DATA_HOME=$HOME/.local/share
